          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Paul in Rome</strong><br>\nPaul eventually reached Rome, where he spent his final years. Tradition holds that he was placed under house arrest while awaiting trial. During this time, he continued to preach and teach, further influencing the spread of Christianity throughout the empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Paul's Martyrdom</strong><br>\nAccording to Christian tradition, Paul was martyred in Rome around the year 67 AD under the emperor Nero. His execution is thought to have been part of Nero's broader campaign of Christian persecution following the Great Fire of Rome in 64 AD.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Paul the Apostle</strong><br>\nPaul's influence on Christianity cannot be overstated. His missionary work, writings, and role in establishing churches throughout the Gentile world have left a lasting mark on Christianity. His theological contributions helped shape the early church and continue to influence Christian thought and practice today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
